@* The Razor side of the static-spelling parity gate. See the remarks on StaticParityView for why the
   pair exists and why it carries no benchmark.

   Written on one line for the reason BenchmarkViewRazor is: newlines between tags become markup frames
   of their own in Razor, and that whitespace difference is an artifact of Razor's source format rather
   than a gap on this side, so it is kept out of the comparison. Unlike BenchmarkViewRazor, every text
   node here is a literal, which is the point — Razor folds this whole subtree into one
   AddMarkupContent frame, and since #140 so does the generator. *@
<div class="card"><h1>Static parity</h1><span>A literal count</span><p>A paragraph of content.</p></div>

@code {
    // Exposes the Razor compiler's render path on the same terms as StaticParityView.Build.
    public void Build(RenderTreeBuilder builder) => BuildRenderTree(builder);
}
